module

public import Riesz2Audit.Repulsion.Definitions

/-!
# Proposition 1.2 (Repulsion of neighbouring particles): the statement

Mathlib-only statement of Proposition 1.2 of J. Boursier, *Decay of correlations and thermodynamic
limit for the circular Riesz gas* (arXiv:2209.00396, revised version 2026).

For every pair of parameters `β > 0`, `s > 0`, `s ≠ 1` (`Parameters`), there is a unique
local total variation limit `P = Riesz_{s,β}` (`UniqueRieszLimit`, `limitingRieszProcess`),
and `PalmRegular P` holds. There are `c, C > 0` such that, for every `i ∈ ℤ` and every
`u ∈ ℝ` with `0 < u ≤ 1`,

`P_{Riesz_{s,β}^0}(z_{i+1}-z_i ≤ u) ≤ C exp(-c u^{-s})` (`repulsionProbability`).

The limit and its Palm regularity are concluded before `c,C` are chosen. The constants are
chosen before the gap label and threshold. The Palm enumeration has `z_0 = 0`
(`rootedPoint`, `rootedGap`).

## How the objects are specified

`Parameters` contains both exponent regimes, with every positive inverse temperature.
`gibbsMeasure` selects the imported companion Gibbs law for `0 < s < 1` and the convergent
lattice-sum Gibbs law for `s > 1`. `microscopicLaw` keeps particles whose centered circle
representatives lie in `(-1/4,1/4)` and rescales their positions by `N`. `UniqueRieszLimit`
asserts existence and uniqueness of a point-process limit in total variation on every
`[-R,R]`, `R > 0`, along `N = n+1`, including that every microscopic law is a probability
measure.

`LineConfiguration` is a locally finite simple subset of `ℝ`, with its σ-algebra generated by
bounded Borel counts. The Palm measure is the average of `Σ_{x∈C∩[0,1)} δ_{C-x}` under `P`
(`palmKernel`, `palmMeasure`). `rootedPalmMeasure` is its pullback to configurations containing
`0` and unbounded in both directions (`RootedConfiguration`). Their increasing enumeration
is defined by infima and suprema (`rootedPoint`), and `rootedGap C i` is `z_{i+1}-z_i`.

`PalmRegular` concludes measurability of the rooted carrier and its Palm mass one, normalization
of the rooted and unrooted Palm measures, zero mass outside the carrier, invariance of the
two-sided gap sequence under an index shift, and integrability and expectation one of every gap.
`repulsionProbability` is the rooted Palm measure of the event `rootedGap C i ≤ u`, with values
in `[0,∞]`. Its upper bound is inserted by `ENNReal.ofReal`. The probability law and the
existence of the limit are conclusions. The constants are chosen for each fixed `β`. The library
also proves the version with constants uniform for `β` in compact intervals,
`Riesz2.repulsion_locallyUniform`, which takes the proved input `External.LogConcaveConvergence`
as an argument.

The statement uses the definitions of `Definitions.lean` in this directory, which imports
Mathlib only. The proof of the theorem is the only `sorry`.
-/

@[expose] public section

namespace Riesz2Audit.Repulsion

noncomputable section

open MeasureTheory Filter Set
open scoped ENNReal NNReal Topology BigOperators BoundedContinuousFunction

namespace Riesz2

/-- For β > 0 and s ∈ (0,1) ∪ (1,+∞), the Palm gaps satisfy P(z_{i+1}−z_i ≤ u) ≤ C exp(−cu^{-s})
for every i ∈ ℤ and 0 < u ≤ 1. The constants c,C > 0 depend only on β and s. The statement
includes the limiting process and its Palm probability law.
This is Proposition 1.2 of the paper. -/
theorem repulsion :
  ∀ p : Parameters, ∃ h : UniqueRieszLimit p,
    let P := limitingRieszProcess p h
    PalmRegular P ∧ ∃ c C : ℝ, 0 < c ∧ 0 < C ∧
      ∀ i : ℤ, ∀ u : ℝ, 0 < u → u ≤ 1 →
        repulsionProbability P i u ≤ ENNReal.ofReal (C * Real.exp (-c * u ^ (-p.val.2))) :=
  sorry

end Riesz2

end

end Riesz2Audit.Repulsion

end
